**Issue**: #433
**Status**: Approved
**Date**: 2026-09-24
**Author**: NMG

Feature: Reverify a repaired implementation without replaying failed evidence
  As an operator of an issue-owned execute controller
  I want a bounded exact-head recheck after a verified source repair
  So that stale failed verification neither blocks delivery forever nor bypasses gates

  @regression
  Scenario: Exact changed-head repair enables a fresh registered gate
    Given a Fail report and matching canonical gate artifact belong to head A under the active verify owner
    And a clean issue-owned repair publishes distinct head B on the same Approved spec and branch
    When the verify worker resumes under that owner
    Then the A report and artifact are archived with exact digests
    And a one-use A-to-B recheck is consumed before the registered gate runs at B

  @regression
  Scenario: Passing evidence advances only from the new head
    Given the changed-head recheck produces complete passing required validations at B
    When acceptance review approves the repaired implementation and normal finalization publishes the report
    Then the report and passed verify handoff bind B
    And the controller may advance to delivery

  @regression
  Scenario Outline: Unproved or consumed recovery does not dispatch
    Given the prior report is Fail or Partial
    And <condition> prevents exact changed-head proof
    When verify recovery is requested
    Then it does not run a new gate or overwrite report evidence
    And it leaves controller and handoff authority unchanged

    Examples:
      | condition                         |
      | the head is unchanged             |
      | the working tree is dirty         |
      | the verify owner is foreign       |
      | the report is a symlink           |
      | the spec identity changed         |
      | the recheck is already consumed   |

  @regression
  Scenario: New non-passing evidence is not promoted
    Given a valid changed-head recheck consumes its one-use authority
    When the registered gate at B fails or remains incomplete
    Then historical A evidence remains archived and B failure stays explicit
    And no passed handoff or delivery dispatch is created

  @regression
  Scenario: Prior same-head external-only incomplete recovery remains independent
    Given an external-only Incomplete artifact remains at its original head
    When its existing one-use prerequisite recheck is requested
    Then its current exact-head and external-only gates remain unchanged
